  "universal-router-2.1.2": {
    "address": "0x23617e59A5925b2A4Bf75d73ff6711cD0b29De85",
    "kind": "router",
    "source": "https://developers.uniswap.org/llms.mdx/docs/protocols/v4/deployments",
    "standingAllowance": {
      "via": "permit2",
      "why": "The router pulls tokens through Permit2 only from the address that called execute, its locker (msgSender() in Dispatcher.sol, set by Lock.sol): Permit2Payments.permit2TransferFrom takes msgSender() as the owner for V2, V3 and V4 swaps with payerIsUser and for PERMIT2_TRANSFER_FROM, and PERMIT2_TRANSFER_FROM_BATCH reverts when a transfer's from is not the locker. It has no owner and no proxy. So a Permit2 allowance to it can be spent only by a later execute the Safe itself makes."
    },
    "ignoresTrailer": "UniversalRouter.execute(bytes,bytes[],uint256) reads only its ABI-decoded arguments: its verified source (contracts/UniversalRouter.sol, Dispatcher.sol and the modules) never reads msg.data or calldatasize, and it takes its caller from msg.sender through Lock.sol, never from calldata as an ERC-2771 contract does.",
    "code": {
      "hash": "0x55e6b334152096d60367d7ab24241948b31e8d0e66adc8b81cba049a19f9d2ac",
      "from": 25999984
    }
  },
